== Notes ==
*To [[quickslot]] protection from good, right-click the quickslot and choose the spell in the radial menu. Dragging the spell from the [[spellbook]] to the quickslot will only place protection from evil there.
*An [[aura of fear]] counts as a mind-affecting spell-like ability.
*This spell is invaluable in a [[PvM]] setting where most monsters have an evil alignment, especially when saving throw auto-failure on 1 is not disabled.
*In a [[PvP]] setting, players often use this spell to protect themselves from both good and evil.
*For immunity to mind spells used by opponents of any (including neutral) alignment, see [[mind blank]] and [[clarity]].
* If a [[potion]] of this spell is made (typically via ''[[brew potion]]''), and if that potion is fed to an [[associate]], then the associate is protected from evil.

